Name: Create main menu window
How to demo: Open program and show a list of 5 options.
Notes: Use java swing

Name: Create 3x3 board
How to demo: In the main menu, click Player vs Player or Player vs Computer and show 9 squares that are clickable
Notes: Use buttons for each square

Name: Create 5x5 board
How to demo: In the main menu, click Arcade and show 25 squares in a grid that are clickable
Notes: Use buttons for each square

Name: Show which player's turn it is
How to demo: During the entirety of the game, it should display X's turn or O's turn in the top left corner depending on whose turn it is
Notes: with maybe some nice looking bars on the screen but maybe not

Name: Show player moves
How to demo: Click a square and show X or O (or in arcade a wall) depending on player turn and power up
Notes: Player take turns in Player vs Player and Arcade, and bot acts as O in Player vs Computer

Name: Computer moves
How to demo: Start a Player vs Computer game and take a turn and see the bot also takes a turn
Notes: it should not be possible to win from the bot

Name: Prevent invalid moves
How to demo: Click an occupied square and see it doesn't change
Notes: Don't allow occupied squares to change

Name: Detect winner
How to demo: Win by having 3 X's or O's in a row (in normal game, and 4 in arcade), horizontally, vertically, or diagonally
Notes: Check rows, columns, diagonals, and display ''Win''

Name: Detect draw
How to demo: Fill the board without a winner
Notes: Display "Draw"

Name: Add turn timer
How to demo: Start a game and show a countdown timer for the current player's turn, starting from 10 seconds
Notes: Timer counts down from 10 each turn and resets when the other player starts their turn
